summary:
  The "this park came over MPRIS" mark is cleared at the bottom of the dispatch
  instead of unconditionally, so four of six early returns leave it standing and
  every later park wears it.

history:
  A Bluetooth speaker powering off sends an AVRCP Pause as its last breath, and
  the widget undoes such a park for the speakers still in the room — right, but
  only while the mark is honest. Both podcast skips and both empty-list returns
  jumped over the single clearing line, so after one media-key pause the mark
  stood for the session. A park made on the widget's own button, the panel icon
  or with Space then read as a dying speaker's breath, and a member leaving
  within two minutes resumed the music over it. The dispatch moved behind a
  try/finally that no return can escape. Found 2026-09-14, chasing issue #13.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          try { _mprisDispatch(cmd); } finally { root._mprisCmdActive = false; }

replace:
          _mprisDispatch(cmd); root._mprisCmdActive = false;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_mpris_origin_flag_cannot_outlive_its_dispatch.
  Line-neutral.
